######## 59ee3fc (empty ROI + hybrid -- args) ########
commit 59ee3fc6da8691bb1a38f11718cd7edb4e05d6a5
Author: Nick Hung <nick@andestech.com>
Date:   Tue Jun 30 10:19:59 2026 +0800

    fix(run): reject empty ROI and hybrid `-- args` (were silently mishandled)

    Two hybrid input bugs found by option fuzzing with hello/gemm, plus the
    help/doc that described them wrong:

    - Empty ROI: `--trigger pc --pc-start X --pc-end X` was accepted, emitting
      enter_pc==exit_pc -- a window that measures nothing (the exit trigger fires
      the instant vsim resumes at the enter PC). Now rejected in hybrid_trigger,
      compared NUMERICALLY so a symbol and its literal 0x address (or 0x0001000
      vs 0x1000) also count as equal.
    - Hybrid `-- args`: fast/cycle forward post-`--` tokens to their single
      engine, but hybrid silently dropped them -- breaking the help's "forward to
      the engine" promise. Hybrid builds BOTH legs' command lines itself, so there
      is no single engine to forward to; reject (rc=2) rather than drop or guess a
      leg. vsim options keep their dedicated flags (--kanata/--objdump).
    - Help/docs: --mem-size's "max 2G" applies only to hybrid's shared mmap; fast
      has no such cap (QEMU's own 16GB limit applies). Correct the run help and the
      USER_GUIDE per-mode table.

    TDD: hybrid_test.cpp (equal-PC, numeric compare); f9 contract (empty ROI,
    no -- args). Unit suite 9/9.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

